                "entry_id": "048f2f6b-ef93-383b-89eb-84ccd5626b9e",
                "word": "rubella",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ca4efae4-c88d-347d-a0a8-837a0f13cfcd",
                        "entry_id": "048f2f6b-ef93-383b-89eb-84ccd5626b9e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A mild disease caused by the Rubella virus infecting the respiratory tract, and characterised by a rash of pink dots, fever and swollen lymph nodes."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ac88d1eb-c8a2-43ab-b961-6a56a828c22a",
                                "sense_id": "ca4efae4-c88d-347d-a0a8-837a0f13cfcd",
                                "text": "At issue is the so-called MMR vaccine, which immunizes children against measles, mumps and rubella, three potentially deadly diseases that were once common and have been mostly wiped out."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "57a88f0d-1ac8-4f3c-8d0c-f6eaf9dace04",
                                "sense_id": "ca4efae4-c88d-347d-a0a8-837a0f13cfcd",
                                "text": "They have congenital rubella syndrome, which they acquired during an outbreak of the rubella virus, or German measles."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
